{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TwuDHx9cv6FcEJUp4qUZgm","type":"tool_result","content":"// Package executor defines the contract for running one agent job somewhere\n// and reporting back. It holds plain data types only and imports nothing from\n// config, state, agent or github, so other executors (Kubernetes, Phase 3)\n// can implement the same five calls.\npackage executor\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"time\"\n)\n\n// Executor runs one agent job. The controller keeps the Handle (as JSON) and\n// passes it back on every call; the executor keeps no durable state.\ntype Executor interface {\n\t// Prepare creates the workspace, writes inputs and opens log files. It\n\t// starts no process.\n\tPrepare(ctx context.Context, j Job) (Handle, error)\n\t// Start launches c without blocking. The ctx does not bound the process:\n\t// only the job deadline and Cleanup stop it.\n\tStart(ctx context.Context, h Handle, c Command) (Handle, error)\n\tStatus(ctx context.Context, h Handle) (Status, error)\n\tLogs(ctx context.Context, h Handle, o LogsOptions) (io.ReadCloser, error)\n\t// Cleanup stops the process if needed and removes the workspace. It never\n\t// deletes logs and is idempotent.\n\tCleanup(ctx context.Context, h Handle, o CleanupOptions) error\n}\n\n// Job describes one run.\n// Network is the role's network setting as the executor sees it.\ntype Network string\n\nconst (\n\tNetworkOn       Network = \"\"         // zero value: today's behaviour\n\tNetworkAdvisory Network = \"advisory\" // role says false; not enforced\n\tNetworkNone     Network = \"none\"     // role says false; enforced (part 2)\n)\n\ntype Job struct {\n\tID         string  // ULID minted at claim; ^[0-9A-Za-z]{1,64}$\n\tRepo       string  // \"owner/repo\"\n\tIssue      int     // 0 = scanner run with no issue\n\tStage      string  // \"scanner\" | \"triage\" | \"worker\" | \"review\"\n\tRole       string  // ^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$\n\tRepoDir    string  // abs path of the controller's clone, already fetched\n\tRef        string  // commit-ish resolved in RepoDir; the worktree is detached at it\n\tRoleDir    string  // abs host path of the role directory\n\tDockerfile string  // abs host path; \"\" = host subprocess\n\tSidecar    Sidecar // zero = none; the executor clones, pins and mounts it read-only\n\tReadOnly   bool    // worktree read-only: Docker mounts :ro, host chmod -R a-w after Prepare\n\tNetwork    Network // from the role's network setting; never from the agent\n\tInputs     []File  // written into the worktree by Prepare\n\t// Scrub lists repo-relative paths Prepare removes from the worktree after\n\t// checkout and before Start, so a file at Ref cannot pass for this job's\n\t// own output. Use it for the job's role file: close-out then trusts that\n\t// file only if it exists, because the agent wrote it. Each path must be a\n\t// file directly under .ard/<Issue>/ (Issue >= 1).\n\tScrub   []string\n\tTimeout time.Duration // > 0\n\t// TrustedInput: the job reads no untrusted input (a deterministic\n\t// scanner); only valid with Stage \"scanner\". The zero value means it\n\t// does, so a builder that forgets the field gets the host-mode warning.\n\tTrustedInput bool\n\t// History: the job may read the repository's full git history, read-only\n\t// (Docker only; host mode does not enforce it),\n\t// at Paths.History (and $ARD_HISTORY). Only valid with Stage \"scanner\".\n\tHistory bool\n}\n\n// Sidecar is a read-only companion repo the executor clones for the job.\ntype Sidecar struct {\n\tName string // config key, for messages\n\tRepo string // \"owner/name\"\n\tRef  string // branch, tag or full 40-hex SHA (gitref.Check)\n}\n\n// File is a worktree-relative file written 0644 by Prepare.\ntype File struct {\n\tPath string\n\tData []byte\n}\n\n// Paths are the locations as the job process sees them. ConfigDir is the\n// job's empty agent-CLI config dir (host: <home>/.claude; Docker:\n// /ard-config); it is empty on a handle stored before it existed.\n//\n// History is the bare clone with all fetched refs, read-only (enforced only by\n// the Docker mount; host mode gives the writable live clone); empty when the\n// job has no History. A Kubernetes executor must supply a read-only copy\n// (for example an init container running git clone --mirror, or a bundle\n// volume) at the same place.\ntype Paths struct{ Work, Role, Sidecar, ConfigDir, History string }\n\n// Command is what to run. Paths must come from Handle.View.\ntype Command struct {\n\tPath string\n\tArgs []string\n\tEnv  []string // \"NAME=value\" secrets; only names the executor allows (AllowEnv)\n\t// Fixed holds non-secret \"NAME=value\" settings the CLI needs (for example\n\t// an agent adapter's config dir). Only names on the executor's AllowFixed\ninternal/worker/run.go:273:\t// s is an agent or fix step here, never a test step.\ninternal/worker/run.go:398:\t\tc = jb.cause(closeout.CauseNoProcess, \"the test step ended abnormally\", false)\ninternal/worker/run.go:648:\t\t\t// A test step has no scrubbed role file and its log is not evidence\ninternal/worker/run.go:650:\t\t\t// code, with the cause the test step ended for.\ninternal/worker/loop.go:114:\t// a test step. nil records nothing.\ninternal/reviewer/run.go:138:\trc := &closeout.ReviewContext{MergeBase: p.base, Added: p.added}\ninternal/closeout/review.go:26:// ReviewContext is what the reviewer loop knows that the role file cannot say.\ninternal/closeout/review.go:29:type ReviewContext struct {\ninternal/closeout/closeout.go:72:\tReview *ReviewContext\ninternal/reaper/finish.go:172:\tReview *closeout.ReviewContext\ninternal/executor/errors.go:10:\tErrForbiddenEnv   = errors.New(\"forbidden environment entry\")\ninternal/executor/executor.go:30:// Network is the role's network setting as the executor sees it.\ninternal/executor/executor.go:31:type Network string\ninternal/executor/executor.go:34:\tNetworkOn       Network = \"\"         // zero value: today's behaviour\ninternal/executor/executor.go:35:\tNetworkAdvisory Network = \"advisory\" // role says false; not enforced\ninternal/executor/executor.go:36:\tNetworkNone     Network = \"none\"     // role says false; enforced (part 2)\ninternal/executor/executor.go:50:\tReadOnly   bool    // worktree read-only: Docker mounts :ro, host chmod -R a-w after Prepare\ninternal/executor/executor.go:51:\tNetwork    Network // from the role's network setting; never from the agent\ninternal/executor/executor.go:98:\tEnv  []string // \"NAME=value\" secrets; only names the executor allows (AllowEnv)\ninternal/executor/executor.go:123:\tReadOnly            bool\ninternal/executor/executor.go:124:\tNetwork             Network // copied from Job by Prepare\ninternal/executor/validate.go:43:\tcase j.Network != NetworkOn && j.Network != NetworkAdvisory && j.Network != NetworkNone:\ninternal/executor/validate.go:44:\t\treturn bad(\"network %q\", j.Network)\ninternal/executor/validate_test.go:36:\t\t{\"network advisory\", func(j *Job) { j.Network = NetworkAdvisory }, true},\ninternal/executor/validate_test.go:37:\t\t{\"network none\", func(j *Job) { j.Network = NetworkNone }, true},\ninternal/executor/validate_test.go:38:\t\t{\"network bogus\", func(j *Job) { j.Network = \"bogus\" }, false},","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e3acb37-8020-42c2-ba96-d30c407bec32","uuid":"9bc87c8b-2232-41cd-8e7a-7021d4e40341","timestamp":"2026-11-24T21:18:49.959Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"// Package executor defines the contract for running one agent job somewhere\n// and reporting back. It holds plain data types only and imports nothing from\n// config, state, agent or github, so other executors (Kubernetes, Phase 3)\n// can implement the same five calls.\npackage executor\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"time\"\n)\n\n// Executor runs one agent job. The controller keeps the Handle (as JSON) and\n// passes it back on every call; the executor 